# Build-time configuration for the production site.
#
# This holds the PostHog project key, and it is committed on purpose.
#
# A PostHog project key is public by design: it is compiled into the JavaScript
# every visitor downloads, so it is readable by anyone who opens the site's
# source no matter where it is stored. Keeping it in Vercel's settings would
# hide it from nobody, while making the build depend on a dashboard field that
# has already been set wrong twice — once as the variable's name instead of its
# value. In the repository it is version-controlled, reviewable, and the build
# cannot silently lose it.
#
# What this key CAN do if someone copies it: send events into this PostHog
# project. That is a nuisance, not a breach — it cannot read anything back.
# What it CANNOT do: read your data, change settings, or touch anything else.
#
# Never put a secret here. Anything prefixed VITE_ is compiled into the bundle
# and is therefore published. Server-side secrets belong in Supabase Edge
# Function secrets, which never reach a browser.
VITE_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_qf4ocNEZoYg7pcgrYtm5rEW7UikTTpfoqVDe6LJETGao
